eland  for retailers for the hospitality sector  the expectation is that this will  sufficiently constrict  that rising trend in case numbers uh in  time  to not perhaps open up fully the country  but to certainly drop down a couple of  levels  for the christmas period so just to  recap uh level five restrictions with a  few exceptions  things uh for example like keeping the  schools open keeping construction going  will kick in uh from midnight on  wednesday here in ireland  uh that means people will have to stay  at home it means the pubs and  restaurants will be restricted only to  delivery or take away  services people will have to stay within  a distance of their home on  on the pain of being fined by the  guardian the irish police we believe  that will be set  at a five kilometer radius so it does  make ireland somewhat of an outlier in  european terms really you'd have to look  to places like the czech republic in  israel  to find similar uh restrictions at the  moment  it's been met with dismay by  restaurateurs hoteliers publicans  and retailers all non-essential retail  will have to close  as well under this plan so a really  drastic move by the irish government  which as i said just a fortnight ago  rejected this course of action but from  midnight on wednesday ireland will be  going back to  what approaches a full lockdown if not  quite
 

